WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.834
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:06.067
You're here. You're watching.
Thank you.

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.567
Well, guys, some big box office
news.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:12.634
The final numbers are in and
"Creed III" just had the biggest

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:15.400
ever opening weekend
for a sports movie.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.901
Biggest ever.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.534
That is a huge deal.

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:23.133
I mean, it almost feels like
a "Miracle."

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:27.801
I bet Michael B. Jordan was
totally "blindsided" by the news

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:31.367
that the movie made over
100 "Million Dollar, Baby,"

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.300
which makes sense.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.934
The "Creed" movies are in
"a league of their own."

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:38.501
The whole time you're like,
will he win?

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:41.334
I think he might.
He "ducks," left, right."

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:43.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.734
He's so "cool, running"
super fast in every montage.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:48.934
So congrats, Michael.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:52.133
It is amazing to see
"Ali's" accomplished --

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.634
"Ali's [all he's]" accomplished.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:57.634
a lot of people thought acting
and directing

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:01.000
might be "rocky" for you,
but you're no "rookie."

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.501
You had confidence to say,
"bring it on."

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:06.067
They weren't sure if you could
take the torch from Stallone,

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.767
but it's official.
You're his true "air, bud."

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:10.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:13.067
Though I got to ask, "Hoosier"
[who's your] accountant?

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:16.300
Because they got to be working
overtime burning

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.934
the "Friday night lights" until
"any given Sunday."

00:01:18.934 --> 00:01:22.467
Anyway, I hope you can relax,
get some "space, jam"

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:25.467
on some other projects and sip
a piña colada with

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:28.200
one of those silly straws where
you can "bend it like Beckham."

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.100
There you go. Thank you.
Congratulations, buddy.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.400
That's right. Come on.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.434
-Come on.
-Thank you very much.

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.901
That's right, "Creed III" had
the biggest opening

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.400
ever for a sports movie.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.133
And I think seeing Michael B.
Jordan has inspired some people

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:46.634
to hit the gym and get in shape.

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:48.534
Check out what I saw earlier
today.

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:51.300
-I signed into law the landmark
American Rescue Plan,

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.067
which provided the resources to
get COVID-19 under control.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.300
-That's interesting, right?

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.634
-Wow.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:02.501
-Speaking of sports,
this is going viral.

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:04.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.701
-He's swollen --
-You have a great laugh.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.334
Whoever's laughing at that,
I love that. Great laugh.

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:09.901
This is going viral.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:11.868
On a recent episode of
"Jeopardy!",

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:14.200
there was a category called
"In the Sport."

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.334
Did you see this today?
-Unh-unh.

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.934
-None of the contestants could
answer any of the questions.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:22.000
This is real.
Take a look at this. Watch this.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.801
-What is roulette?

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.434
[ Buzzer ]
-That would be polo.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.734
[ Buzzer ]
That's hockey.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.200
[ Buzzer ]
That's boxing.

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:49.467
-What is water polo?

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:50.968
[ Buzzer ]
-That's golf.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.267
[ Buzzer ]
That's baseball.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:00.834
[ Laughter ]
-Wow!

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.801
That was so funny.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:07.067
Yep, that beloved American
sport, roulette.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.267
-Ah.
-That's a great sport.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:11.501
